"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n\n<head>\n  <base target=\"_top\">\n</head>\n\n<body>\n  <div class=\"fep-events\">\n    <div class=\"event-filters mb-4\">\n      <div class=\"input-group mb-3\">\n        <div class=\"input-group-prepend mr-2\">\n          <span class=\"input-group-text\">Filters</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"btn-group-toggle event-type-selector\" data-toggle=\"buttons\">\n                    <label class=\"btn btn-secondary\" data-selector=\"event-free\">\n            <input type=\"checkbox\">Free        </label>\n                    <label class=\"btn btn-secondary\" data-selector=\"event-general-public\">\n            <input type=\"checkbox\">General Public        </label>\n                    <label class=\"btn btn-secondary\" data-selector=\"event-hybrid\">\n            <input type=\"checkbox\">Hybrid        </label>\n                    <label class=\"btn btn-secondary\" data-selector=\"event-in-person\">\n            <input type=\"checkbox\">In Person        </label>\n                    <label class=\"btn btn-secondary\" data-selector=\"event-service-provider\">\n            <input type=\"checkbox\">Service Provider        </label>\n                    <label class=\"btn btn-secondary\" data-selector=\"event-service-providers\">\n            <input type=\"checkbox\">Service Providers        </label>\n                    <label class=\"btn btn-secondary\" data-selector=\"event-virtual\">\n            <input type=\"checkbox\">Virtual        </label>\n                  </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-general-public event-free event-virtual\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\">Employer of the Day: Davcor Aviation Services</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Virtual</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Free</span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Monday November 16, 2026 1:00 PM - 2:00 PM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          Davcor is hiring for several aviation opportunities in Everett, including Aircraft Fuel Systems Technician 1, Aircraft Avionics Maintenance Technician, Aircraft Quality Inspector, Aircraft Maintenance Supervisor, and A&amp;P Aircraft Mechanic. The Fuel Systems Technician role is full-time, entry-level, pays $19–$22 per hour, and includes training; no prior aviation experience is required. <br><br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://us06web.zoom.us/meeting/register/TengBWG0TDKiD26FlU1Rmg#/registration\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n        General Public      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-service-providers  event-virtual\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\">Washington State Health Care Authority: Trauma-informed Care for Career Services Series - Part 1</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Virtual</span><span class=\"ml-3\"></span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Tuesday November 17, 2026 8:30 AM - 10:00 AM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          The Washington State Health Care Authority (HCA) Foundational Community Supports (FCS) team invite you to join them and Rutgers Department of Psychiatric Rehabilitation and Counseling Professions for a four-part series on Trauma-Informed Care (TIC). <p>This four-part webinar series will explore how trauma can affect a person’s experience with career services, looking for work, and being successful on the job. We’ll talk about what trauma can look like in everyday interactions and how providers can respond in ways that build trust, safety, and connection.</p><p>The series will focus on practical strategies that providers can use in supported employment, including job development, placement, coaching, and retention. We’ll also look at how trauma can affect workplace skills, communication, stress, and job success. Participants will be introduced to tools such as cognitive restructuring that can help individuals work through thoughts and challenges that may get in the way of their employment goals. Attendees will leave each webinar with practical ideas they can use with the people they support.</p><p>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://rutgers.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_aMT_WnpBST2AsgC3HQkwpA#/registration\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n         Service Providers      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-general-public event-free event-virtual\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\">WSAC Financial Aid Webinar</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Virtual</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Free</span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Tuesday November 17, 2026 5:30 PM - 6:30 PM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          This session is offered in English and Spanish / esta presentación está disponible en inglés y español.<br><br>Join the 12th Year Campaign to learn more about financial aid and take your first step creating your StudentAid.gov account (FSA ID) or WASFA account at this event.  Please only use your initials instead of your full first and last name when you register. <br><br> Únase a la campaña del duodécimo año para obtener más información sobre la ayuda financiera y dé el primer paso para crear su FSA ID o cuenta WASFA en este evento.  Utilice únicamente sus iniciales en lugar de su nombre y apellido cuando se registre.  <br><br>Registration required.<br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://wsac-wa-gov.zoom.us/meeting/register/7Rkfcjg1ThadFs2XuFpYjQ#/registration\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n         General Public      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-general-public event-free event-hybrid\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\">WorkSource WIOA Orientation</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Hybrid</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Free </span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Wednesday November 18, 2026 1:00 PM - 2:00 PM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          Please join us virtually or onsite at WorkSource Everett to learn more about the Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act. We will spend the first hour (1pm - 2pm) with an information session, with the following hour (2pm - 3pm) reserved for time if you'd like to connect with a Career Advisor with any additional questions. If you have any questions or concerns, please reach out to our team at <a href=\"mailto:info@snococareers.com\">info@snococareers.com</a><br><br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://worksource.my.site.com/worksourcewa/events/event-details?eventId=a0Tcs00002echgdEAA\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n        General Public      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-general-public event-free event-virtual\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\">WSAC Parent &amp; Caregiver Financial Aid Night</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Virtual</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Free</span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Wednesday November 18, 2026 5:30 PM - 6:30 PM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          Join us as we talk about types of financial aid, how students apply, and the parent's role in the application process. Staff from the Washington Student Achievement Council will be there to answer your questions. <br>Únase a nosotros mientras hablamos sobre los tipos de ayuda financiera, cómo los estudiantes la solicitan y el papel de los padres en el proceso de solicitud. El personal del Washington Student Achievement Council estará allí para responder sus preguntas. <br><br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://wsac-wa-gov.zoom.us/meeting/register/Bs-wWEGbQQyk9GRFiMqwLQ#/registration\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n        General Public      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-general-public event-free event-virtual\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\">Disability Workshop</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Virtual</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Free</span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Thursday November 19, 2026 10:00 AM - 11:00 AM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          Virtual Drop-in Lab for People with a Disability Seeking Employment or Help Staying in the Workforce. Returning to work, or staying in the workforce, can be difficult with a disability or chronic health condition. We are here to answer disability related questions regarding work, including strategies to disclose disabilities, request accommodations, and optimize disability benefits.<br><br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://us02web.zoom.us/j/84597487795?pwd=JQRz6vRHge2elwqY1TcgqevtfTY76b.1\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n        General Public      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-general-public  event-in-person\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\">Resume Writing Workshop</span><span class=\"ml-3\">In Person</span><span class=\"ml-3\"></span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Friday November 20, 2026 12:00 PM - 1:45 PM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          Join ODAT (One Day at a Time) for this supportive hands-on workshop. You'll work toward a draft resume and cover letter tailored to a specific job and walk away with practical tools for reviewing and improving both. This is a live event with no registration required. Here's the address for the event:<br><br>2720 Rucker Ave, #5<br>Everett, WA 98275        </p>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n         General Public      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-general-public event-free event-in-person\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\">Employer of the Day: Family First at Home</span><span class=\"ml-3\">In-person</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Free</span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Monday November 23, 2026 1:00 PM - 2:45 PM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          Employer of the Day – Family First at Home Join us at WorkSource Everett on Monday, November 23, 2026, from 1:00–3:00 PM to meet the hiring team from Family First at Home! Family First at Home is hiring Caregivers, Home Care Aides (HCAs), and Certified Nursing Assistants (CNAs) to provide compassionate in-home care that helps individuals maintain their independence and quality of life. Current Opportunities: Full-time and part-time caregiver positions Starting pay: $22.25–$25.00 per hour, depending on experience, certifications, and region Additional $1 per hour for weekend shifts Paid HCA training and orientation Flexible schedules and opportunities for professional growth Benefits including a 401(k) with company match, same-day pay options, and employee referral bonuses HCA or CNA certification is preferred, but not required. Come meet the team, learn about available positions, ask questions, and explore career opportunities with Family First at Home!<br><br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://worksource.my.site.com/worksourcewa/events/event-details?eventId=a0Tcs00002f9DqDEAU\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n        General Public      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-service-provider event-free event-hybrid\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\"> Washington Financial Coaching Network</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Hybrid</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Free</span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Wednesday November 25, 2026 2:00 PM - 3:00 PM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          A peer-learning community for financial coaches and navigators across the state. Held on the4th Wednesday of each month, the meeting provides a collaborative space to:<ul><li>Share     Best Practices: Discuss effective coaching techniques, program strategies,     and client engagement tools.</li></ul><ul><li>Resource     Sharing: Exchange up-to-date information on local community resources,     financial products, and social services that support     low-to-moderate-income residents.</li></ul><ul><li>Peer     Support &amp; Collaboration: Build professional connections, troubleshoot     client challenges with fellow practitioners, and reduce isolation among     coaches across non-profit, housing, and social service agencies.</li></ul><ul><li>Skill     Building: Stay informed on emerging trends in financial empowerment,     consumer protection, and state-level economic resources.</li></ul><p>Click on link to attend.</p><br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://us02web.zoom.us/j/81360579953?pwd%3Di5lQisGwDgzPDKIxcS7JGnTs6rSD9J.1&amp;amp;sa=D&amp;amp;source=calendar&amp;amp;ust=1792256234339087&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw2Izl4lfHHWFiJTZosH0DlR\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n        Service Provider      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-general-public event-free event-virtual\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\">WSAC Financial Aid Webinar</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Virtual</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Free</span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Tuesday December 1, 2026 5:30 PM - 6:30 PM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          This session is offered in English and Spanish / esta presentación está disponible en inglés y español.<br><br>Join the 12th Year Campaign to learn more about financial aid and take your first step creating your StudentAid.gov account (FSA ID) or WASFA account at this event.  Please only use your initials instead of your full first and last name when you register. <br><br> Únase a la campaña del duodécimo año para obtener más información sobre la ayuda financiera y dé el primer paso para crear su FSA ID o cuenta WASFA en este evento.  Utilice únicamente sus iniciales en lugar de su nombre y apellido cuando se registre.  <br><br>Registration required.<br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://wsac-wa-gov.zoom.us/meeting/register/OmW0Qm5DT6G5uLAQo5tfgQ#/registration\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n         General Public      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-general-public event-free event-virtual\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\">WSAC Parent &amp; Caregiver Financial Aid Night</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Virtual</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Free</span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Wednesday December 2, 2026 5:30 PM - 6:30 PM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          Join us as we talk about types of financial aid, how students apply, and the parent's role in the application process. Staff from the Washington Student Achievement Council will be there to answer your questions. <br><br>Únase a nosotros mientras hablamos sobre los tipos de ayuda financiera, cómo los estudiantes la solicitan y el papel de los padres en el proceso de solicitud. El personal del Washington Student Achievement Council estará allí para responder sus preguntas. <br><br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://wsac-wa-gov.zoom.us/meeting/register/_M0QX8XwQdm_6bLlcFXLJA#/registration\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n        General Public      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-service-provider event-free event-hybrid\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\">Helping ALICE Move from Survival to Abundance</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Hybrid</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Free</span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Thursday December 10, 2026 10:00 AM - 11:30 AM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          A peer-learning community for financial coaches and navigators across the state. Held on the4th Wednesday of each month, the meeting provides a collaborative space to:<ul><li>Share     Best Practices: Discuss effective coaching techniques, program strategies,     and client engagement tools.</li></ul><ul><li>Resource     Sharing: Exchange up-to-date information on local community resources,     financial products, and social services that support     low-to-moderate-income residents.</li></ul><ul><li>Peer     Support &amp; Collaboration: Build professional connections, troubleshoot     client challenges with fellow practitioners, and reduce isolation among     coaches across non-profit, housing, and social service agencies.</li></ul><ul><li>Skill     Building: Stay informed on emerging trends in financial empowerment,     consumer protection, and state-level economic resources.</li></ul><p>Click on link to attend.</p><br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://everyoneiswelcome.app.neoncrm.com/nx/portal/neonevents/events?path=%2Fportal%2Fevents%2F59432\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n        Service Provider      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-service-providers  event-virtual\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\">Washington State Health Care Authority: Trauma-informed Care for Career Services Series - Part 2</span><span class=\"ml-3\"> Virtual</span><span class=\"ml-3\"></span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Tuesday December 15, 2026 8:30 AM - 10:00 AM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          The Washington State Health Care Authority (HCA) Foundational Community Supports (FCS) team invite you to join them and Rutgers Department of Psychiatric Rehabilitation and Counseling Professions for a four-part series on Trauma-Informed Care (TIC).<br>  <br>This four-part webinar series will explore how trauma can affect a person’s experience with career services, looking for work, and being successful on the job. We’ll talk about what trauma can look like in everyday interactions and how providers can respond in ways that build trust, safety, and connection.<br><br>The series will focus on practical strategies that providers can use in supported employment, including job development, placement, coaching, and retention. We’ll also look at how trauma can affect workplace skills, communication, stress, and job success. Participants will be introduced to tools such as cognitive restructuring that can help individuals work through thoughts and challenges that may get in the way of their employment goals. Attendees will leave each webinar with practical ideas they can use with the people they support.<br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://rutgers.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_aMT_WnpBST2AsgC3HQkwpA#/registration\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n         Service Providers      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-general-public event-free event-virtual\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\">Financial Capabilities: Making Changes with My Money</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Virtual</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Free </span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Tuesday December 15, 2026 2:30 PM - 4:30 PM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          Making Changes with My Money<ul><li>Learn to set achievable short and long-term goals</li><li>Evaluate your habits and whether they are helping you to reach those goals</li><li>Understand how our emotions can affect how we manage our money</li><li>Learn about banks and other financial institutions</li></ul><p>If you need an accommodation to participate in this event, please contact Liza Neal at <a href=\"mailto:Liza.Neal@esd.wa.gov\" target=\"_blank\">Liza.Neal@esd.wa.gov</a> or WA Relay Services at 711 prior to the event</p><br><br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://worksource.my.site.com/worksourcewa/events/event-details?eventId=a0Tcs00002Z1TIxEAN\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n        General Public      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-service-provider event-free event-hybrid\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\"> Washington Financial Coaching Network</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Hybrid</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Free</span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Wednesday December 23, 2026 2:00 PM - 3:00 PM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          A peer-learning community for financial coaches and navigators across the state. Held on the4th Wednesday of each month, the meeting provides a collaborative space to:<ul><li>Share     Best Practices: Discuss effective coaching techniques, program strategies,     and client engagement tools.</li></ul><ul><li>Resource     Sharing: Exchange up-to-date information on local community resources,     financial products, and social services that support     low-to-moderate-income residents.</li></ul><ul><li>Peer     Support &amp; Collaboration: Build professional connections, troubleshoot     client challenges with fellow practitioners, and reduce isolation among     coaches across non-profit, housing, and social service agencies.</li></ul><ul><li>Skill     Building: Stay informed on emerging trends in financial empowerment,     consumer protection, and state-level economic resources.</li></ul><p>Click on link to attend.</p><br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://us02web.zoom.us/j/81360579953?pwd%3Di5lQisGwDgzPDKIxcS7JGnTs6rSD9J.1&amp;amp;sa=D&amp;amp;source=calendar&amp;amp;ust=1792256234339087&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw2Izl4lfHHWFiJTZosH0DlR\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n        Service Provider      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-service-providers  event-virtual\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\">Washington State Health Care Authority: Trauma-informed Care for Career Services Series - Part 3</span><span class=\"ml-3\"> Virtual</span><span class=\"ml-3\"></span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Tuesday January 19, 2027 8:30 AM - 10:00 AM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          The Washington State Health Care Authority (HCA) Foundational Community Supports (FCS) team invite you to join them and Rutgers Department of Psychiatric Rehabilitation and Counseling Professions for a four-part series on Trauma-Informed Care (TIC).<br>  <br>This four-part webinar series will explore how trauma can affect a person’s experience with career services, looking for work, and being successful on the job. We’ll talk about what trauma can look like in everyday interactions and how providers can respond in ways that build trust, safety, and connection.<br><br>The series will focus on practical strategies that providers can use in supported employment, including job development, placement, coaching, and retention. We’ll also look at how trauma can affect workplace skills, communication, stress, and job success. Participants will be introduced to tools such as cognitive restructuring that can help individuals work through thoughts and challenges that may get in the way of their employment goals. Attendees will leave each webinar with practical ideas they can use with the people they support.<br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://rutgers.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_aMT_WnpBST2AsgC3HQkwpA#/registration\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n         Service Providers      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-service-provider event-free event-hybrid\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\"> Washington Financial Coaching Network</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Hybrid</span><span class=\"ml-3\">Free</span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Wednesday January 27, 2027 2:00 PM - 3:00 PM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          A peer-learning community for financial coaches and navigators across the state. Held on the4th Wednesday of each month, the meeting provides a collaborative space to:<ul><li>Share     Best Practices: Discuss effective coaching techniques, program strategies,     and client engagement tools.</li></ul><ul><li>Resource     Sharing: Exchange up-to-date information on local community resources,     financial products, and social services that support     low-to-moderate-income residents.</li></ul><ul><li>Peer     Support &amp; Collaboration: Build professional connections, troubleshoot     client challenges with fellow practitioners, and reduce isolation among     coaches across non-profit, housing, and social service agencies.</li></ul><ul><li>Skill     Building: Stay informed on emerging trends in financial empowerment,     consumer protection, and state-level economic resources.</li></ul><p>Click on link to attend.</p><br><br>        </p>\n                <a href=\"https://us02web.zoom.us/j/81360579953?pwd%3Di5lQisGwDgzPDKIxcS7JGnTs6rSD9J.1&amp;amp;sa=D&amp;amp;source=calendar&amp;amp;ust=1792256234339087&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw2Izl4lfHHWFiJTZosH0DlR\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Attend</a>\n              </div>\n      <div class=\"card-footer\">\n        Audience:\n        Service Provider      </div>\n    </div>\n        <div class=\"card mb-4 event-show event-service-providers  event-virtual\">\n      <h4 class=\"card-header d-flex\">\n        <span class=\"mr-auto\">Washington State Health Care Authority: Trauma-informed Care for Career Services Series - Part 4</span><span class=\"ml-3\"> Virtual</span><span class=\"ml-3\"></span>\n      </h4>\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\n        <h5 class=\"card-title\">\n          Tuesday February 16, 2027 8:30 AM - 10:00 AM        </h5>\n        <p class=\"card-text\">\n          The Washington State Health Care Authority (HCA) Foundational Community Supports (FCS) team invite you to join them and Rutgers Departmen